# Structure Refinement and Validation

## Overview

Structure refinement and validation are essential steps in protein modeling to improve the quality of predicted three-dimensional (3D) 
structures and assess their reliability. Refinement optimizes the protein model by improving its geometry, while validation evaluates the
accuracy and stereochemical quality of the refined structure. In this project, GalaxyRefine was used for structure refinement, and the
refined models were validated using PROCHECK, ERRAT, and Verify3D.

## Objective

To refine the predicted protein structure and evaluate its quality using multiple validation tools.

## Methodology

The predicted protein structure was first refined using GalaxyRefine to improve its structural quality. The refined model was then 
validated using PROCHECK for stereochemical analysis, ERRAT for non-bonded interaction assessment, and Verify3D for sequence–structure 
compatibility evaluation.

## Input

* Predicted protein structure (.pdb).

## Output

* Refined protein structure (.pdb).
* Ramachandran plot.
* ERRAT quality factor.
* Verify3D assessment report.

## Applications

* Protein model refinement.
* Structure quality assessment.
* Preparation for molecular docking.
* Structural biology research.

## Files Included

* Predicted protein structure (.pdb).
* Refined protein structure (.pdb).
* PROCHECK, ERRAT, and Verify3D reports.

## Conclusion

Structure refinement and validation improved the quality of the predicted protein model and confirmed its reliability through multiple
validation metrics, making it suitable for downstream structural and functional analyses.

